1	// Shared plumbing for this pack's speech-API checks. The two general helpers
2	// every check needs — `finding` and `stripComments` — come from the engine's own
3	// helpers; what stays here is the part specific to reading speech-API call sites.
4	
5	// What counts as shipped browser source. Deliberately NOT a path root: every
6	// rule in this pack is gated on the speech API it judges actually appearing in
7	// the file, so the trigger is the API usage itself and the scan can be repo-shape
8	// agnostic. A path scope hard-wired to one project's layout would make every rule
9	// match zero files — and pass VACUOUSLY GREEN — in a repo laid out differently,
10	// which is the worst failure mode a check has.
11	//
12	// The one thing the scan must still exclude is test scaffolding: hand-rolled
